@startuml action-namespace-registration
!theme plain
title Action vocabulary (v1.3): a handler declares its actions, the owner (or an agent with registry.actions.register) registers the namespace, grants and commands may then name it; example github-runner.*

participant "Runner helper\n(privileged process, own identity)" as HB
participant "Key keeper" as KK
participant "Trust registry\n(keys, grants, action namespaces)" as T
actor "Owner\n(client app, root key)" as OW
participant "Admin orchestrator\n(grant registry.actions.register, prefix ops.*)" as AO
participant "Our bridge\n(trust gate)" as BR

== 1. the handler declares itself ==
HB -> KK: sign handler-manifest/1 {actions github-runner.{start,stop,restart,register}\nwith argument schemas, target form host:mini/runners/<runner>, effects irreversible}
KK --> HB: signature (identity of the helper)
HB -> T: publish manifest

== 2. the namespace is registered ==
alt by the owner
  OW -> T: action-namespace/1 {namespace github-runner.*, handler runner-helper,\nmanifest_sha256, hosts [host:mini], grantable_by [root, role:admin]} signed by root
else by an agent under a delegable grant
  AO -> KK: sign action-namespace/1 {namespace ops.deploy.*, handler ..., ...}
  KK --> AO: signature
  AO -> T: record + grant chain (registry.actions.register, prefix ops.*)
  T -> T: verify chain to the root; prefix allowed? not session.* etc.
  alt outside the agent's prefix
    T --> AO: refused{prefix}
  else inside
    T -> T: append
  end
end
T -> T: same name again: only the same handler, or a root-signed replacement;\nremoval = revocation record

== 3. grants and commands name it ==
OW -> T: grant G1 {subject K_alexis, actions [github-runner.restart, stop],\ntargets [host:mini/runners/*], conditions caveats/v1 (hours, max_per_hour),\ndelegable depth 1}
T -> T: issue-time check: every action in G1 is registered → accept\n(a grant on an unregistered action is refused at issue)
note over BR
  Later, a command with action github-runner.restart is checked at the gate
  against the manifest's argument schema and the grant chain, then passed
  to the registry-named handler (see delegated-action-handler).
end note
@enduml
